DESCRIPTION:The Dr. Grier Williams School of Music and UWF Gulf Coast Cultu
 re Series presents Songs of Revolution & Rebellion\, a USO-style variety s
 how that takes audiences on a musical journey through revolution\, rebelli
 on\, war\, peace\, patriotism and protest on Thursday\, October 22\, at 5:
 30 p.m. at the Museum of Commerce.\n\nFrom the American Revolution and Civ
 il War through the World Wars and beyond\, faculty\, students and guest pe
 rformers bring history to life through songs\, letters\, stories and humor
 . The program pairs music from different eras with reflections on the peop
 le who fought\, served\, sacrificed and challenged the nation to live up t
 o its ideals—from Abigail Adams' call to "remember the ladies" to soldie
 rs' letters home\, wartime songs of hope and later voices of change.\n\nPa
 rt of the Songs of Revolution & Rebellion: A USO-Style Variety Show explor
 es a recurring American story: Every generation inherits a nation still in
  progress\, and has a role in determining what comes next.\n\nInspired by 
 the tradition of USO entertainment\, the show also pays tribute to Pensaco
 la's deep connection to the U.S. military and its identity as the Cradle o
 f Naval Aviation. The evening concludes with a special recognition of acti
 ve-duty service members\, veterans and military families.\n\nFeatured perf
 ormers include: Corey McKern-Baritone\, April Kocher-Soprano\, Sheila Dunn
 -Soprano\, Dylan Fischer-Baritone\, Coda Lee Owens-Baritone\, Ethan Middle
 ton-Baritone\, Blake Riley-Collaborative Pianist\, Rachel Bettis-Flute\, T
 he Blue Anchor Belles.\n\nSeating is limited. Registration is recommended.
 \n\nThis event is presented by the UWF College of Arts\, Social Sciences a
 nd Humanities Gulf Coast Culture Series\, The Dr. Grier Williams School of
  Music\, and is sponsored in part by the John C. Pace Symposium Series.
GEO:30.408434;-87.211378
LOCATION:Museum of Commerce
SUMMARY:Gulf Coast Culture Series Presents Songs of Revolution & Rebellion:
  A USO-Style Variety Show
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.uwf.edu/event/songs-of-revolution-rebellion-a-
 uso-style-variety-show
CATEGORIES:Special Event
CATEGORIES:Performance
END:VEVENT
