DESCRIPTION:Monty\, a charming but poor young man finds out he is ninth in 
 line for an earldom and a family fortune when his mother passes away. His 
 chance of outliving those ahead of him in succession are slim\, so he deci
 des to take matters into his own hands. Of course\, murder isn’t the onl
 y thing on his mind\, he must also decide which woman should become his br
 ide: the honorable Phoebe or fiery Sibella. Based on the 1907 fictional no
 vel “Israel Rank: The Autobiography of a Criminal” by Roy Horniman\, t
 his four-time Tony Award-winning musical is filled with murder\, wit\, and
  laughs with book and lyrics by Robert L. Freedman and music and lyrics by
  Steven Lutvak.\n\nDue to Adult situations and subject matter\, this show 
 may not be appropriate for all audiences.\n\nDepartment of Theatre
GEO:30.545533;-87.217429
LOCATION:Building 82 - Center for Fine and Performing Arts\, Besser Studio 
 Theatre
SUMMARY:A Gentleman's Guide to Love and Murder
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.uwf.edu/event/a-gentlemans-guide-to-love-and-m
 urder
CATEGORIES:Performance
END:VEVENT
